across Germany demanding improvements in education, climate and affordability. Protesters say they aren't being taken seriously and will keep protesting until things change.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lufthansa to cut 1,000 jobs, citing ongoing losses — reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ae29afeabe546af55a31ddd294ea7e30fce271f6aa9ee31b609705595d5917d</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062--a7b4260396ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a letter obtained by the media, Lufthansa's executive board said the German company is losing €20 million every month. In addition to job cuts, operational cuts are also planned.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Pistorius visits Auschwitz memorial in Poland trip</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4de4b6d06ee166adcf3858b9bd3d8bd4006af54fb2015a4f15552711da3edd0e</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-pistorius-visits-auschwitz-memorial-in-poland-trip/live-79987991--a7bef4a1dbc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-pistorius-visits-auschwitz-memorial-in-poland-trip/live-79987991?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's defense minister's first stop in Poland was the memorial site of the former Nazi extermination camp Auschwitz-Birkenau. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wadephul: 'Coalition of the Willing' talks in Berlin send strong signal to Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0130dbfa108e9153e845fdf30e87ef72db62a713a07c6a6fc890e693435f3ed1</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664--ce1ce93ebd6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Wadephul has said the Coalition of the Willing meeting in Berlin sends a clear message to Moscow to take peace talks seriously. He also warned Ukraine should be prepared for peace talks to fail.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can German auto manufacturing recover after Mercedes and VW cuts?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dd7a73c8477028a188490fa3eb1a9ba25e78061f662e0341d4cab90bc68b3b2</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928--88277c189f1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German automakers are pulling back on investments at home, sparking fresh anxiety about the auto sector's future. Some industry watchers think there is still a narrow window to stem the decline. But how?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany face belgium in Nations League quarterfinals — Klopp plays down favorites tag</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a5a02677c59e0b00fd7b33867d67e0a1e42b6b59b51b705fb33fbeba6958fa8</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-face-belgium-in-nations-league-quarterfinals-klopp-plays-down-favorites-tag/a-80004794--66b2cbbf524d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-face-belgium-in-nations-league-quarterfinals-klopp-plays-down-favorites-tag/a-80004794?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp is looking to "carry positive momentum forward" as his team draw neighboring Belgium in the quarterfinals of the UEFA Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Zverev faces fresh lawsuit from ex-girlfriend</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f11028cd1d123dbe1e535f3e43c6ef231aa149ff0603e97343069518c2aa1a88</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005--d63dbeaa4aae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World No. 1 tennis player Alexander Zverev is facing a new lawsuit related to a domestic abuse trial. The lawyer for his ex-girlfriend, Brenda Patea, told DW what the allegations are against the German player.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
